   "widgets_values": [
    "## ACE-Step 1.5 XL SFT (dev copy) - the licence-clean quality upgrade\n\n**Why it exists:** the user's ears call the shipped flow's audio not fantastic, and that flow is ACE-Step 1.5\n**turbo** - **8 steps, cfg 1**. XL is the same family at 4B with a **50-step, cfg 7** recipe, and **MIT**\nlicence, so it is the one candidate that could raise quality without a licence regression.\n\n**Built flat from the shipped `audio_ace_step1_5_xl_sft.json`**, mirroring its wiring exactly: `UNETLoader` ->\n`ModelSamplingAuraFlow` (shift 3) -> `KSampler`; the text encoder's whole widget list is **read verbatim from\nthe template** so its `cfg_scale`/temperature/top_p are upstream's own; the seed feeds the encoder *and* the\nsampler; the duration feeds the latent *and* the encoder; negative is the positive through\n`ConditioningZeroOut`. The template's frontend-only `PrimitiveNode`/`PrimitiveInt` become\n`FloatConstant`/`INTConstant` (a hand-built graph cannot carry frontend primitives).\n\n**Inputs:** the shared comparison input - the industrial style + 'Iron heart' lyric read from the shipped cover\nflow - seed 31, 120 s. So this take is directly comparable with `ace_iron` (the turbo baseline on the same\ntext and seed) and with the MiniMax take.\n\n**Files:** `acestep_v1.5_xl_sft_bf16.safetensors` (9.97 GB) in `models/diffusion_models/`,\n`qwen_0.6b_ace15.safetensors` + `qwen_4b_ace15.safetensors` in `models/text_encoders/`, `ace_1.5_vae.safetensors`\nin `models/vae/` - all MIT (`Comfy-Org/ace_step_1.5_ComfyUI_files`).\n\n**Knobs:** steps/cfg (the quality lever against the turbo), `ModelSamplingAuraFlow` shift, the text encoder's\n`cfg_scale`, and the shared style/lyric/seed/duration.\n"
   ],
